      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Log in",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "**What it does**\n\nExchanges a username and password for an access token (a JWT valid for 1 hour). The test script saves it in the `token` collection variable, and every other request sends it as `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}`.\n\n**Input**\n\n- Headers: `Content-Type: application/json`\n- Body:\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `username` | string | yes | Case-sensitive. |\n| `password` | string | yes | |\n\n```json\n{\"username\": \"demo\", \"password\": \"demo-password\"}\n```\n\n**Output**\n\n| Status | When | Body |\n|---|---|---|\n| `200` | Valid credentials. Comes with `Cache-Control: no-store`. | `{\"access_token\": \"eyJ...\", \"token_type\": \"Bearer\", \"expires_in\": 3600}` |\n| `401` | Wrong username or password. Same response in both cases, so it doesn't reveal which users exist. | `{\"error\": \"invalid_credentials\"}` |\n| `422` | A field is missing, empty or not a string. | `{\"error\": \"invalid_params\", \"details\": {\"username\": \"must be a non-empty string\"}}` |\n| `400` | The body is not a JSON object. | `{\"error\": \"invalid_json\"}` |\n| `415` | The `Content-Type` is not `application/json`. | `{\"error\": \"unsupported_media_type\"}` |\n| `413` | The body is larger than 16 KB. | `{\"error\": \"payload_too_large\"}` |\n\n`expires_in` is the token lifetime in seconds. When the token expires, log in again."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', body.access_token);",
                  "pm.test('token saved for the other requests', () => pm.expect(body.access_token).to.be.a('string'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
