    {
      "name": "Products",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create product",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/products",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "products"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"{{productName}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "**What it does**\n\nAsks for a product to be created **about 5 seconds later**. It doesn't create the product: it records a *creation request* and schedules a background job that creates it. Follow the request with **Get creation status** (the test script saves its id in `requestId`).\n\nIt is **idempotent by name**: a user can't have two products with the same name (compared case-insensitively), so sending the same name again never creates a second product.\n\n**Input**\n\n- Headers: `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}`, `Content-Type: application/json`\n- Body:\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `name` | string | yes | 1 to 255 characters. Leading and trailing spaces are removed. Unique per user, ignoring case. |\n\n```json\n{\"name\": \"Termo\"}\n```\n\n**Output**\n\nThe body is the creation request:\n\n| Field | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `id` | Request id, to follow it with **Get creation status**. |\n| `name` | Product name. |\n| `status` | `pending`, `completed` or `failed`. |\n| `product_id` | The created product's id once `completed`, otherwise `null`. |\n| `error` | Why it `failed`, otherwise `null`. |\n| `created_at` | When it was requested (ISO 8601, UTC). |\n\n| Status | When |\n|---|---|\n| `202` | New name, or a request for this name is already pending (the same request is returned). Comes with `Location: /products/requests/{id}` and `Retry-After: 5`. |\n| `200` | The product already exists: returns the completed request that created it. |\n| `422` | The name is missing, empty, not a string or longer than 255 characters. |\n| `503` | The job queue is down. The request is recorded as `failed`, so retrying later is safe. |\n| `401` | Missing, invalid or expired token. |\n| `400` / `413` / `415` | Body not a JSON object / larger than 16 KB / wrong `Content-Type`. |"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('accepted (202) or already exists (200)', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 202]));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('requestId', pm.response.json().id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
