        {
          "name": "Get creation status",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/products/requests/{{requestId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "products",
                "requests",
                "{{requestId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**What it does**\n\nReturns the status of a creation request made with **Create product**. A request is `pending` for about 5 seconds and then becomes `completed` (or `failed`). Uses the `requestId` saved by **Create product**.\n\n**Input**\n\n- Headers: `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}`\n- Path parameter:\n\n| Parameter | Type | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `id` | integer | The request id (`id` in the **Create product** response, or the end of its `Location` header). |\n\n**Output**\n\n| Status | When | Body |\n|---|---|---|\n| `200` | The request exists and belongs to the user. | The creation request (same fields as **Create product**). |\n| `404` | No request with that id for this user. Another user's request is also reported as not found. | `{\"error\": \"not_found\"}` |\n| `401` | Missing, invalid or expired token. | `{\"error\": \"invalid_token\"}` |\n\n`status` values:\n\n- `pending`: the product will be created shortly.\n- `completed`: the product exists, and its id is in `product_id`.\n- `failed`: the product was not created, and `error` says why. It can be `name_taken` (a product with that name appeared first), `queue_unavailable` (the job queue was down) or `processing_failed` (the creation kept failing after several retries). A new request for the same name can be made."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "console.log('status:', pm.response.json().status);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
