    {
      "name": "Error examples",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Log in with a wrong password",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"wrong-password\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "**What it does**\n\nShows the response to a failed login. A wrong password and a username that doesn't exist get exactly the same response, so it can't be used to find out which users exist.\n\n**Input**\n\n- Headers: `Content-Type: application/json`\n- Body: `{\"username\": \"{{username}}\", \"password\": \"wrong-password\"}`\n\n**Output**\n\n`401 Unauthorized` with `{\"error\": \"invalid_credentials\"}`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "401 Unauthorized",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "Content-Type",
                    "value": "application/json"
                  }
                ],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth",
                  "host": [
                    "{{baseUrl}}"
                  ],
                  "path": [
                    "auth"
                  ]
                },
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"wrong-password\"\n}",
                  "options": {
                    "raw": {
                      "language": "json"
                    }
                  }
                },
                "auth": {
                  "type": "noauth"
                }
              },
              "status": "Unauthorized",
              "code": 401,
              "header": [
                {
                  "key": "Content-Type",
                  "value": "application/json"
                }
              ],
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "body": "{\n  \"error\": \"invalid_credentials\"\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "List products without a token",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/products",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "products"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "**What it does**\n\nShows what happens when a protected endpoint is called without a token. Every endpoint except `/auth`, `/health` and `/AUTHORS` requires one.\n\n**Input**\n\nNo `Authorization` header (the request's auth is set to *No Auth*).\n\n**Output**\n\n`401 Unauthorized` with `{\"error\": \"missing_token\"}` and the header `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. With an invalid or expired token, the code is `invalid_token`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "401 Unauthorized",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/products",
                  "host": [
                    "{{baseUrl}}"
                  ],
                  "path": [
                    "products"
                  ]
                },
                "auth": {
                  "type": "noauth"
                }
              },
              "status": "Unauthorized",
              "code": 401,
              "header": [
                {
                  "key": "Content-Type",
                  "value": "application/json"
                },
                {
                  "key": "WWW-Authenticate",
                  "value": "Bearer"
                }
              ],
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "body": "{\n  \"error\": \"missing_token\"\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create product with an empty name",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/products",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "products"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "**What it does**\n\nShows a validation error: the name must be a non-empty string of at most 255 characters.\n\n**Input**\n\n- Headers: `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}`, `Content-Type: application/json`\n- Body: `{\"name\": \"\"}`\n\n**Output**\n\n`422 Unprocessable Content`. Validation errors list each invalid field in `details`:\n\n```json\n{\"error\": \"invalid_params\", \"details\": {\"name\": \"must be a non-empty string of at most 255 characters\"}}\n```"
          },
